Craig can rename the words on a bay, for example a Hoist bay to Bay 8.
The pencil is on the planner bay header and is shown to a controller (stored as operator) or an administrator.
Saving calls public.set_workshop_bay_display_name(uuid, integer, text).
That function updates display_name only, bumps version, and writes audit_events.
A blank name writes the station name plus " - Bay NN".
id, code, bay_number, ordering and bookings are not written.

Screens that build a label from the station and the padded bay number now use display_name first:
Workshop Planner headers, toasts and the vehicle side panel, the Control Board bay row, and Close gaps (already on bay_display_name).

Pins stay 241. No expected_function_md5 row was added.

Check bay_display_name_visual_only runs inside pdc_ops.fault_regression_check under search_path pg_catalog.
It renames Hoist bay 2 (HOIST-BAY-02) inside a block that rolls back, then checks the id, code, bay number and booking count, and that workshop_bay_display_label returns Bay 8.

